From: ImWebBrowser
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore/Soup: don't let content sniffer downgrade empty-body
 script responses to text/plain

The libsoup content sniffer guesses a MIME type from the response body.
For an empty body (Content-Length: 0) there is nothing to sniff, and the
sniffer falls back to "text/plain", overriding the server-declared
"application/javascript". ES module loading then fails with
"TypeError: 'text/plain' is not a valid JavaScript MIME type.",
aborting SPA boot (seen with NVIDIA's login CDN serving 0-byte chunks
during deploys).

When the server declares a supported JavaScript MIME type and the
response body is empty, keep the declared type instead of the sniffer's
guess.
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/network/soup/ResourceResponseSoup.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/network/soup/ResourceResponseSoup.cpp
@@ -62,9 +62,20 @@
 
     String contentType;
     const char* officialType = soup_message_headers_get_one(responseHeaders, "Content-Type");
-    if (!sniffedContentType.isNull() && m_httpStatusCode != SOUP_STATUS_NOT_MODIFIED && sniffedContentType != officialType)
-        contentType = String::fromLatin1(sniffedContentType.data());
-    else
+    if (!sniffedContentType.isNull() && m_httpStatusCode != SOUP_STATUS_NOT_MODIFIED && sniffedContentType != officialType) {
+        // The content sniffer can only make a useful guess when there is actual
+        // content; for an empty body it falls back to a "text/plain" guess that
+        // would downgrade a server-declared script MIME type and break ES module
+        // loading (ScriptModuleLoader rejects non-JS MIME types). NVIDIA's login
+        // CDN transiently serves 0-byte JS chunks during deploys, so keep the
+        // declared script type for empty-body responses and let dynamic
+        // import() succeed instead of aborting the SPA boot.
+        String official = String::fromLatin1(officialType);
+        if (MIMETypeRegistry::isSupportedJavaScriptMIMEType(official) && !soup_message_headers_get_content_length(responseHeaders))
+            contentType = official;
+        else
+            contentType = String::fromLatin1(sniffedContentType.data());
+    } else
         contentType = String::fromLatin1(officialType);
     setMimeType(extractMIMETypeFromMediaType(contentType));
     if (m_mimeType.isEmpty() && m_httpStatusCode != SOUP_STATUS_NOT_MODIFIED)
